WEBVTT

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:03.725
Security operations use OT telemetry in several ways.

00:00:03.725 --> 00:00:06.700
Detection engineering turns known conditions into maintained alerts.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.700
Threat hunting asks focused questions across historical data.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:13.200
Anomaly detection identifies deviation from expected behavior,

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.410
while incident response reconstructs identities, assets, communication, changes,

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:18.300
and process impact.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.770
The same telemetry can update asset inventory.

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:24.700
Newly observed devices, changed peers, dormant systems returning to service,

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:28.070
and unexpected protocols should be validated and assigned ownership.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:31.770
Vulnerability teams can use observed reachability, asset function,

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.995
and dependencies to improve prioritization.

00:00:33.995 --> 00:00:36.085
A useful investigation joins sources.

00:00:36.085 --> 00:00:40.360
A remote-access session, firewall connection, engineering-workstation logon,

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:43.960
controller interaction, and historian trend may describe one operational story.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:48.100
Reliable time and consistent asset identifiers make that correlation possible.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:53.400
SOC alerts need OT context: site, zone, asset role, criticality, protocol or action,

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:57.279
maintenance state, supporting evidence, and the team that can validate process meaning.

00:00:57.279 --> 00:01:01.590
Generic severity without this information shifts work to the analyst and increases unsafe

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:02.400
assumptions.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.600
Escalation should connect security with operations and engineering.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:09.030
They can distinguish a cyber event from equipment failure, planned maintenance,

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:12.400
or process transition and can advise which containment actions are safe.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:16.700
Automated isolation should be used cautiously where it could remove control, visibility,

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:17.600
or redundancy.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.300
Every investigation should improve the telemetry program.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:24.295
Correct asset records, repair collection gaps, tune detections, preserve new indicators,

00:01:24.295 --> 00:01:25.295
and update runbooks.

00:01:25.295 --> 00:01:28.780
Telemetry creates value when it moves from collection to shared evidence,

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:30.940
coordinated decisions, and measurable improvement.
